    },
    {
     "_key": "00000000002b",
     "_type": "block",
     "children": [
      {
       "_key": "000000000027",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "For those seeking a more luxurious rail experience, the Watania Egypt Sleeping Train offers two daily services to "
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000029",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [
        "000000000028"
       ],
       "text": "Cairo"
      },
      {
       "_key": "00000000002a",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": ", departing at 5 pm and 7 pm. Prices per person or double cabin (fits two) include dinner and breakfast, with rates of US$60 and US$120, respectively."
      }
     ],
     "markDefs": [
      {
       "_key": "000000000028",
       "_pendingInternalRef": {
        "sourceLocale": "en",
        "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/history-of-cairo/"
       },
       "_type": "externalLink",
       "href": "/guide/cairo/history-of-cairo",
       "newTab": false
      }
     ],
     "style": "normal"
    },
    {
     "_key": "00000000002d",
     "_type": "block",
     "children": [
      {
       "_key": "00000000002c",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "So, whether you prefer the swift ascent of air travel, the scenic route by bus, the communal camaraderie of servees, or the classic charm of a train journey, Kom Ombo awaits your arrival, promising a journey that is as memorable as the destination itself."
      }
     ],
     "markDefs": [],
     "style": "normal"
    },
    {
     "_key": "00000000002f",
     "_type": "block",
     "children": [
      {
       "_key": "00000000002e",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": " By Bus: A Scenic Ride"
      }
     ],
     "markDefs": [],
     "style": "h2"
    },
    {
     "_key": "000000000031",
     "_type": "block",
     "children": [
      {
       "_key": "000000000030",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": " By Servees: Communal Connections"
      }
     ],
     "markDefs": [],
     "style": "h2"
    },
    {
     "_key": "000000000039",
     "_type": "block",
     "children": [
      {
       "_key": "000000000032",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "Servees and minibusses can be found at the bus station, the same location as the buses. To "
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000034",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [
        "000000000033"
       ],
       "text": "reach the station"
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000035",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": " from the train station, a taxi ride costs E£15 or E£0.50 in a communal taxi. Communal taxis are a budget-friendly option. A seat in a servees or minibus to Luxor will set you back E£18, while the journey to Kom Ombo costs E£7, and the route to "
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000037",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [
        "000000000036"
       ],
       "text": "Edfu"
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000038",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": " is priced at E£15."
      }
     ],
     "markDefs": [
      {
       "_key": "000000000033",
       "_pendingInternalRef": {
        "sourceLocale": "en",
        "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/reaching-siwa-egypt/"
       },
